"""
## Purpose and audience

Executable evidence for the closed `@rt(hal)` compiler binding table, written
for the compiler engineers who own the MC/DC + RT/HAL hardening lane and for
reviewers deciding whether a HAL operation may compile as executed code on a
given host.

## Operator workflow

Run this spec and confirm the Results line reports 0 failed. Every scenario
first proves the drafted binding module is still absent (fail-closed
tripwire, see Compatibility), then documents one slice of the drafted table:
provider-mask parsing, the clock/file/stream/environment/random/socket
binding entries, the device execution ABI, and the extraction metadata.

## Compatibility and limitations

The drafted module `compiler.common.hal.rt_hal_static_binding` (functions
`rt_hal_static_binding_v1`, `rt_hal_manifest_provider_mask_v1`,
`rt_hal_manifest_operation_v1`, `rt_hal_provider_mask_compares_v1`,
`rt_hal_manifest_is_static_direct_v1`,
`rt_hal_binding_signature_diagnostic_v1`,
`rt_hal_binding_signature_key_diagnostic_v1` and
`rt_hal_binding_requires_device_execution_route_v1`) does not exist anywhere
under `src/` (verified by content grep at authoring time), so the drafted
lookup table cannot be driven yet. Each scenario is a fail-closed tripwire:
it passes only while the drafted source file is absent and goes RED the day
the module lands, forcing the drafted assertions (preserved verbatim in each
body) to be restored and executed.

## Verification guidance and troubleshooting

If a scenario goes RED, the drafted binding module now exists: restore the
commented drafted assertions in that scenario, replace the tripwire probe,
and re-run. If every scenario fails on an empty read rather than the
tripwire oracle, check that the working directory is the repository root.
"""
# Lifecycle: research: doc/01_research/local/mcdc_rt_hal_hardening.md ; plan: doc/03_plan/sys_test/mcdc_rt_hal_hardening.md ; architecture: doc/04_architecture/mcdc_rt_hal_hardening.md ; design: doc/05_design/mcdc_rt_hal_hardening.md
# @feature mcdc_hal_runtime_hardening
# @manual_section: closed rt(hal) static bindings

use std.spec.step

use std.spec.{describe, it, expect}

extern fn rt_file_read_text(path: text) -> text

fn drafted_module_absent() -> bool:
    val drafted = rt_file_read_text("src/compiler/common/hal/rt_hal_static_binding.spl") ?? ""
    drafted == ""

describe "closed @rt(hal) compiler bindings":
